{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "oan-da-charts",
    "name": "OAN DA Charts",
    "description": "Central dashboard Visit chart feeder (Confluence Dashboard APIs contract).\n\nBase path: /api/v1/da-services\n\nRoute: GET /charts/visits → **raw JSON array** (no status/data envelope).\nChart id for BFF: `visits`\n\n## Auth\nKeycloak staff realm client-credentials + role `charts:read`.\nLeave `charts_client_id` empty for local (Charts Auth Enabled unchecked on DA Services Settings).\nWhen client id is set, the collection pre-request fetches a token from `charts_token_url`.\n\n## Query params\n| Param | Env key | Notes |\n|-------|---------|-------|\n| region, zone, woreda, kebele | same | Empty / `all` = no filter |\n| from, to | same | Inclusive calendar days on `scheduled_at`. Both omitted → current month |\n| da_id, visit_type, status | same | Optional equality (`status` → `physical_status`) |\n| groupBy | groupBy | Omit → one KPI object. Else `visit_type` \\| `woreda` \\| `da_id` \\| `month` |\n\n## Docs\ndocs/charts-visits-integration.md",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const clientId = pm.environment.get('charts_client_id') || pm.collectionVariables.get('charts_client_id') || '';",
          "const secret = pm.environment.get('charts_client_secret') || '';",
          "const tokenUrl = pm.environment.get('charts_token_url') || '';",
          "if (!clientId || !secret || !tokenUrl) { return; }",
          "const existing = pm.environment.get('access_token');",
          "if (existing) { return; }",
          "pm.sendRequest({",
          "  url: tokenUrl,",
          "  method: 'POST',",
          "  header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },",
          "  body: {",
          "    mode: 'urlencoded',",
          "    urlencoded: [",
          "      { key: 'grant_type', value: 'client_credentials' },",
          "      { key: 'client_id', value: clientId },",
          "      { key: 'client_secret', value: secret }",
          "    ]",
          "  }",
          "}, function (err, res) {",
          "  if (err) { console.warn('charts token request failed', err); return; }",
          "  const body = res.json() || {};",
          "  if (body.access_token) {",
          "    pm.environment.set('access_token', body.access_token);",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', body.access_token);",
          "  }",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8200" },
    { "key": "charts_client_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "access_token", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Health (no token)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/da-services/health",
            "description": "Open health check — no charts token required."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Health 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test(\"Envelope status success\", function () {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql(\"success\");",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.service).to.eql(\"da_services\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "Healthy",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
                "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/da-services/health"
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "body": "{\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"message\": \"Success\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"status\": \"healthy\",\n    \"service\": \"da_services\",\n    \"api_version\": \"v1\"\n  },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"api_version\": \"router\"\n  }\n}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Visits chart",
      "description": "GET /charts/visits — raw KPI array for BFF chart id `visits`. Sample bodies captured against local site with Charts Auth Enabled unchecked (counts reflect that site's visit data).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Visits KPI (default month)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/da-services/charts/visits",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "da-services", "charts", "visits"]
            },
            "description": "No query params → current calendar month, all geo. Returns one KPI object (zeroed if no matches)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test(\"Body is a JSON array\", function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(Array.isArray(pm.response.json())).to.be.true;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"KPI keys present when ungrouped\", function () {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (!body.length) return;",
                  "  const row = body[0];",
                  "  [\"planned\",\"completed\",\"missed\",\"rescheduled\",\"in_progress\",\"cancelled\",\"total\",\"farmers_reached\"].forEach(function (k) {",
                  "    pm.expect(row).to.have.property(k);",
                  "  });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "Ungrouped KPI (current month)",
